## How to File a Correction

When a downstream bot produces a wrong answer traceable to a wiki page:

1. Identify the specific wiki page that sourced the wrong claim
2. File an entry below in this format:
   ```
   [YYYY-MM-DD] wiki/<path/to/page.md>
     Wrong: [the incorrect claim]
     Correct: [the right answer]
     Source: [what proves the correction — source page, raw file, external reference]
     Action: [whether the page was updated; what changed]
   ```
3. Edit the corrected wiki page with the accurate information
4. Update the page's `source-date:` frontmatter to today's date
5. Add a `GAP:` note if the correction revealed a broader gap

